Implement separate runtime-use and administration grants; enforce view access and current revocation at discovery and execution. All owner fields derive from trusted context. If static credentials remain, explicitly map them to provisioned user/grant using stable identifiers rather than hash(token). Acceptance: normal MCP credentials cannot edit config or arbitrary commands; restricted client cannot invoke hidden tools by guessed names; grant revocation takes effect on subsequent calls. Admission policy and ownership authorization are independent; broadening OAuth login must not broaden grants.
